"notes": "Cash basis. Beginning cash = total governmental funds beginning fund balance 9,238,274 (cash basis, equals beginning net position); ending cash = 10,140,579 (p3). Governmental funds statement p4 Total Governmental Funds column used for receipts/disbursements. Transfers in/out each 10,139,297 (net zero). No business-type funds. General Fund budget schedule reports a combined Taxes line 9,369,327; split using General Fund column on p4 (property 8,147,590; motor vehicle 501,435; nameplate 661,876; other 58,426); split item labels altered to show the split. Intergovernmental may include federal/state/local mix; categorized as intergovernmental/state aid. General Fund and Inheritance/Road schedules list by department/function only (no object breakdown), so detail_category is 'not itemized'; the printed 'Miscellaneous' General Government line (1,869,134) stays miscellaneous expenditure with review. Noxious Weed Control (listed under Public Works on the p5 schedule) is natural resources/conservation in detail; the p4 statement Public Works line stays streets/highways because it is not separable there. Nonmajor funds recorded from the combining statement Total column only (pp11-13; individual fund granularity not captured; more detailed than the budget schedules on pp8-10, not double counted). Report inconsistency: budget schedule p9 shows Disaster Fund receipts actual 2,107,319 while combining statement p12 shows 2,170,319; combining statement used. Other financing lines in detail are signed as printed. Re-extracted from scratch with every page re-read. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
